data: {"text":"1. That the Applicant has been falsely implicated in FIR No. 124/2026 dated 15.03.2026, registered at Police"}

data: {"text":" Station Kotwali, under Sections 303 and 351 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, and"}

data: {"text":" is presently languishing in judicial custody since 16.03.2026.\n\n2. That the Applicant submits that he"}

data: {"text":" has been falsely implicated in the aforesaid FIR due to a pre-existing land dispute with the Complainant. The instant"}

data: {"text":" case appears to be a result of malicious prosecution arising out of civil"}

data: {"text":" disputes between the parties regarding property rights and boundaries.\n\n3. That the Applicant"}

data: {"text":" was not present at the time of the alleged incident and has credible witnesses who can establish his alibi. The Applicant was elsewhere attending to his legitimate business and"}

data: {"text":" can produce documentary evidence and witness testimony to substantiate his whereabouts during the material"}

data: {"text":" time of the alleged occurrence.\n\n4. That the Applicant was arrested on 16.03.2026 and has been in continuous judicial custody since then,"}

data: {"text":" thereby already undergoing detention for a considerable period. The continued incarceration of the Applicant without trial"}

data: {"text":" would amount to pre-trial punishment, which is violative of the fundamental principles of criminal"}

data: {"text":" jurisprudence.\n\n5. That the Applicant has no criminal antecedents and is a law-abiding citizen of good reputation in"}

data: {"text":" society. He has never been involved in any criminal activity in the past and maintains clean records with the law enforcement agencies."}

data: {"text":" His character and conduct have always been exemplary and above board.\n\n6. That the Applicant has deep roots"}

data: {"text":" in the community and has no intention or inclination to flee from justice or evade the legal"}

data: {"text":" process. He has permanent residential address, family ties, and business interests"}

data: {"text":" in the locality, which serve as sufficient sureties for his appearance before the Court as and"}

data: {"text":" when required.\n\n7. That the Applicant undertakes to cooperate fully with the investigation process and will make himself"}

data: {"text":" available before the investigating agency as and when called upon. He will not tamper with any evidence or influence"}

data: {"text":" any witnesses in the case and will abide by all conditions that this Hon"}

data: {"text":"'ble Court may deem fit to impose.\n\n8. That the continued detention of the Applicant in judicial custody would be a gross violation of his fundamental right to life"}

data: {"text":" and personal liberty as guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of India. The right to bail is inher"}

data: {"text":"ent in the presumption of innocence until proven guilty, which is a cardinal principle of criminal law"}

data: {"text":".\n\n9. That considering the nature of allegations, the evidence on record, and the fact that one of the off"}

data: {"text":"ences under Section 351 BNS is bailable in nature, the Applicant has made out"}

data: {"text":" a prima facie case for grant of bail. The investigation is pending and the Applicant's liberty should not be curt"}

data: {"text":"ailed indefinitely pending completion of the investigation.\n\n10. That the Applicant undertakes to abide by all terms and conditions that this"}

data: {"text":" Hon'ble Court may impose while granting bail and will not misuse the liberty"}

data: {"text":" granted to him. He will remain present for all court proceedings and will not leave the jurisdiction without prior permission of the Court."}

